+# Performance and battery audit fixes — 1.21.69 (code 292)
+
+Status: **source-only. Not compiled, not unit-tested, not device-tested.** The authoring environment had no Android SDK and no Gradle dependency access; each edited Kotlin file was only syntax-parsed. Expect to fix any compile error on first build.
+
+## Changes
+
+| Area | Change | Why |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `AppPreferences` | `lastPositionMs` moved to a second tiny DataStore (`listen_to_music_resume_position`). `values` no longer carries it; `current()` merges it; `resumePosition` flow and `resumePositionMs()` fall back to the legacy key until the first save. | The 5 s save used to rewrite the whole preferences file, re-decode every JSON blob and publish a new `UserPreferences` (root/`settings` recomposition) while playing. |
+| `MainViewModel` | Holds `resumePositionMs` from `preferences.resumePosition`; `playNow` uses it. Position ticker polls at 2 s while not playing (500 ms while playing). | Player events already publish state changes immediately. |
+| `StackPlaybackCoordinator` | Ticker runs at 50 ms only while playing or gated; otherwise idles at 250 ms (`STACK_IDLE_TICK_MS`) and is woken at once by `play()` and seeks through a conflated channel. | Paused sessions no longer wake at 20 Hz. |
+| `VideoAmbientColors` | Polls every 2 s (not 900 ms) when no video surface is a candidate. | Process-lifetime loop. |
+| `PlaybackMotion` / `NowPlayingScreen` | `AnimatedWaveformBars` gains a `() -> Float` overload read in the draw phase; the animated progress is held as `State`, so the slider and labels no longer recompose every frame. The slider thumb now follows the 2 Hz position publish. | Per-frame recomposition on Now Playing. |
+| `NowPlayingScreen` lyrics | Per-line `AnnotatedString` is `remember`ed; only the active line depends on position. | Rebuilt for every visible line at each tick. |
+| `AppBackground` | `ambientBackdrop` is composed only inside `AmbientBackdropBox`, where it is shown. | It was built (colour sampling, histogram, three colour animations) even when a live video covered it. |
+| `MainViewModel.importM3u` | `HashMap` lookups for `content://` and cue-clip entries (same first-match semantics). | Per-entry linear scans. |
+
+## Deliberately not changed
+
+- Thumbnail scroll gating (`ThumbnailRequestScheduler.setPaused`, `ThumbnailRepository.checkpoint`): pausing all thumbnail work during scroll is intentional from the Library work in 1.21.67/68. Allowing disk reads during a fling is a trade-off that needs a device trace first.
+- Already fixed upstream in 1.21.67/68: scheduler single-pass pump, viewport range snapshots, per-row graphics layer, `isPlaying` plumbing.
+- `TextureView` video surfaces, `inspectElement` as a `Modifier.Node`, Nodes draw allocations, baseline profile / macrobenchmark, swallowed-exception counters: need device measurements or SDK tooling.
+
+## Verify before release
+
+1. `python3 scripts/validate-greater-art-version.py`, JVM tests, lint, `assembleRelease`.
+2. Upgrade install: resume position survives (legacy key fallback), then pause/kill/resume.
+3. Stack: pause, resume, seek while paused; start-gate latency unchanged.
+4. Now Playing: waveform progress smooth, slider thumb acceptable on short tracks.
+5. A/B battery and gfxinfo/Perfetto runs against 1.21.68 (screen off paused, screen off playing, Stack paused).
